        "procedure": "To 2 (0.529 g, 0.5 mmol) was added H3SiPh (0.108 g, 1 mmol) in Et2O (10 mL) at room temperature. After stirring 2 h, the pale yellow solution was concentrated and allowed to stand at room temperature for several days to precipitate a crystalline product. The mother liquor was removed; residual oily PhSiH2CH2SiMe3 was dried under vacuum and the residue dissolved in hexane. Concentration to a small volume and standing at room temperature for several days gave colorless crystals of 3·2hexane, which afforded 3 as a white powder after drying. Alternatively, 3 was obtained almost quantitatively by recrystallization of 4 from hexane.",
